        verification storyQuotedWordsAreBoundedDoD : Test { :>> id = "a5997c9a-fc86-496e-a28c-7b51fc5b99c3"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DELIVERED: checks::quoted_spans (keel-cli/src/view/checks.rs) extracts every quoted span from a note with declared boundaries - typographic “…” and ‘…’ pairs, and an ASCII apostrophe that OPENS only when the previous character is not alphanumeric and CLOSES only when the next character is not a letter, so `brief's` and `let's` never open or close a span; an unclosed opener yields nothing; quotes_conversational_words answers from that list, and view::read_back_names reads the same spans, so the id/option/title match runs over what the human said and only that. `keel accept <d> --words TEXT [--note framing]` (main.rs fold_words_into_note) folds their words into the note as `{framing} - their words, verbatim: “{words}”`, making the boundary declared by construction; the CliCommand fact and usage carry the new form. VERIFIED: checks::tests::quoted_spans_are_bounded_and_an_in_word_apostrophe_never_opens_one - the live refused note from issue397 now yields exactly the human's marked line; a spliced note whose apostrophe-shifted span would carry the decision id while the human's words do not yields only the human's words (the passing-direction case, constructed); contractions and an unclosed opener yield nothing; view::tests::read_back_names_the_decision_or_refuses gains the live note binding for d0360, the spliced note refused, and “c for d375” binding to d0375 by digits and by letter; delegated_records_must_quote_or_cite_a_gesture still holds. LIVE: the acceptance of D0375 itself was recorded through the fix - `keel accept d0375 --words 'c for d375' --by wweatherholtz` - and read back by id and option letter. Resolves issue397."; }
        // RAN: keel suite . 589/0 (receipt 37f6d8356120); the three tests named in the DoD pass; keel accept d0375 --words recorded the live acceptance; keel validate . 689 clean; keel guard --no-receipt ALL PASS; CLAUDE.md accept paragraph carries --words and the declared-boundary rule
