    verification quotedWordsAreBoundedStandupGate : Test { :>> id = "37a3fc79-78ff-4454-a512-d8aa2e2cad41"; :>> title = "Sprint 606 standup gate"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-08"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "ONE CHOICE: fix the extractor AND add a declared-boundary flag, rather than either alone. The extractor alone still asks the recorder to hand-quote correctly and leaves the ASCII apostrophe doing two jobs; the flag alone leaves every existing --note path with the old splitter, which is where the refusal actually fired. With both, the flag is the path an agent should take and the extractor is the control when it does not. A second choice: an in-word apostrophe is decided by its neighbours (alphanumeric before / letter after), not by a dictionary of contractions - a possessive on a record id (d0360's) has a digit before it and must not open either."; }
