    verification quotedWordsAreBoundedReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "ccf97c77-449b-4ab2-975e-c7d56f83eac9"; :>> title = "Sprint 606 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-08"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "THREE QUESTIONS (D0172). Can a span now be attached to words the human did not say? Only if the recorder places a declared opener before text that is not theirs - the same fabrication the quote rule already cannot detect and D0289 leaves to the human's exception; what is closed is the ACCIDENTAL splice, where a correct quote is read at the wrong boundary. Does the tightening refuse anything it should accept? A standalone ASCII 'quote' still opens; typographic pairs open; the only newly-silent shape is an in-word apostrophe, which never began a human's words. What is NOT claimed: that the check judges consent (it reads back a referent, D0375 option C's plan-covers-step rule is the next item); that guards under the keystone lock changed (checks.rs is the accept path's reader, guards.rs is untouched)."; }
